# Unit 397: verify router, Rules and Closing checklist cut to the phase-wide rules (V1, QT-01, QT-02); When it runs cites nzt-plan (V3); data mechanism read from the stack (V2)
run after the slice was built, or interleaved because the user asked => router When it runs; nzt-plan Building the plan step 2: "unless the user asks for it"
plan written and approved before execution, naming each scenario's target => router The stop that comes first; test-design The plan is approved before anything runs
qa ✓ only where every built area's scenarios passed on their latest run => test-run Marking qa on the story: "qa ✓ when the latest run of every scenario covering that criterion passed, for every area marked ✓"
data mechanism agreed with the user and recorded in the stack document => test-data Done when: "The mechanism was agreed with the user and is recorded in the stack document"
every scenario that needed data has its setup and teardown scripts, and every teardown that did not run is recorded as data debt => test-data Done when (first and fifth points)
what this session can drive was checked, and no screen scenario was resolved with api evidence => router Which component, and with what: "Then check what this session can actually drive"; "A UI scenario is never marked passed on API evidence"
every scenario has a status from the closed vocabulary => test-run Recording the run: "Closed vocabulary"; Done when: "Every scenario has a dated run with its state"
every blocked carries a cause you genuinely could not resolve => test-data The data is yours to create: "blocked is for what you cannot resolve"; test-run Done when: "or is blocked with its cause"
criteria with no scenario listed in the index => test-design Traceability: "A criterion with no scenario appears as no scenario"; router Where it lands: index lists "criteria with no scenario"
evidence saved per run and referenced from the results table => test-run Evidence: "One folder per run, referenced from the results table"
bugs filed with their state, and none of them silently fixed here => router Done when: "every failure has its bug file"; bug.md Three states; test-run Done when: "Nothing was repaired mid-run"
index updated: last run, result, open bugs, what is automated, data left behind => router Where it lands, index line
a failure stops the batch => plan slices.md When QA fails inside the batch; test-run Do not fix while testing: "a run with a failure also stops the batch"
how its data is obtained => test-design The scenario: Data and Setup / cleanup lines
the data mechanism is agreed there too, once => router: "The data mechanism is the stack's Test data opt-in"; test-data Ask the mechanism once (V2)
design the cases before running anything => test-design opening: "written and approved before anything is executed"; router Rules: "The expected result comes from the requirement"
closed status vocabulary => test-design The scenario and test-run Recording the run: "Closed vocabulary"
you generate the test data, with the mechanism the user chose => test-data The data is yours to create
every scenario that needs data gets two scripts, written before the run: one that prepares it and one that deletes exactly what the first one created => test-data Two scripts per scenario, written together
blocked is for what you cannot resolve, not for what you did not think to create => test-data The data is yours to create: "blocked is for what you cannot resolve, never for what you did not think to create"
run through the real entry point => test-run Through the real entry point; Success is not persistence
coverage runs both ways => test-design Traceability, both ways
a re-run adds a dated execution; it never overwrites the previous one => test-run Recording the run: "A retest adds a dated run; it never overwrites the previous one"
the bug has three states => bug.md Three states, not two
do not fix a defect while testing => router Rules: "Finding a defect and repairing it are different units"; test-run Do not fix while testing
